0,Jicarilla Apache - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jicarilla_Apache,"The term jicarilla comes from Mexican Spanish meaning ""little basket"", [4] referring to the small sealed baskets they used as drinking vessels. To neighboring Apache bands, such as the Mescalero and Lipan, they were known as Kinya-Inde (""People who live in fixed houses"").","Apache, Jicarilla",Eyak-Athabaskan
